# Line endings — canonical form in this repository is LF (.editorconfig
# already declares end_of_line = lf, but editors are not the checkout path).
#
# Without this file, Git for Windows' default core.autocrlf=true rewrites
# text files to CRLF at checkout. gofmt's canonical output is LF, so
# `make verify`'s fmt-check then reported essentially every Go file as
# unformatted and both Windows CI legs died before any real check ran
# (reproduced locally: an autocrlf=true checkout flags 229 files; the
# committed tree is pure LF). Attributes override core.autocrlf, so this
# makes a Windows checkout byte-identical to a Linux one.
* text=auto eol=lf
